{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "In overlapping categories, Keski-Pohjanmaa's crude MDT-recorded share, 1.4% (95% CI 0.4–4.8), is below 6.0% nationally; crude curative treatment, 22.3% (95% CI 16.3–29.7), is not distinguishable from 27.0%.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded",
        "cty:curative:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:curative"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "In 2019–2023, a multidisciplinary team (MDT) meeting was recorded for a crude share of 1.4% (95% CI 0.4–4.8; n=2/148) of new patients in Keski-Pohjanmaa, where the 95% confidence interval excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873); however, HILMO captures specialist procedures only from direct patient contacts, so MDT records measure recording practice rather than care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories where a patient may receive several treatments, Keski-Pohjanmaa's crude shares are 22.3% (95% CI 16.3–29.7; n=33/148) vs 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally for curative treatment, 32.4% (95% CI 25.4–40.3; n=48/148) vs 30.4% (4522/14873) for life-prolonging treatment, and 46.6% (95% CI 38.8–54.6; n=69/148) vs 39.5% (5871/14873) for symptomatic treatment, with every 95% confidence interval including its national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:symptomatic:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public registry data do not show when treatment started or measure referral and primary-care waits, while preliminary, unpublished figures report an average of 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland (compared with 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark), comprising 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Taulukko 11 reports only crude county shares that are neither age-adjusted nor stage-adjusted, as stage is missing for about 48% of patients, and public data omit key pathway timestamps.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "q:7885b0974f",
        "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Taulukko 11 gives crude county shares with separate limitations: they are not age-adjusted (county age-adjusted shares appear only in Kuva 16, where digitised national curative reference lines read from the figure are 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women, ±0.5 percentage points) and, separately, they cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "fig:age_adjusted_only_kuva16",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Keski-Pohjanmaa, the crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 25.0% (95% CI 18.7–32.5; n=37/148), whose 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.5% (4089/14873); this category mixes untreated patients and treatment that was not recorded, while a journal article found about 90% HILMO–Cancer Registry concordance for diagnoses only.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "lit:hilmo_90"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data in the report do not measure symptom onset or referrals, primary-care visits are not included in the report's data, occupational health is not mentioned, imaging appears only indirectly as the basis of diagnosis in approximately 20% of patients, and HILMO shows whether a specialist visit occurred within 12 months (93.6%) but not when.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "To address data blind spots and delays, the team recommends publishing county stage, drug, and MDT coding coverage, tracking THL 21/2016 access times, and standardising referrals and diagnostic coordination.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:950a2f797b",
        "q:556431a0c2"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because Keski-Pohjanmaa's crude MDT-recorded share is 1.4% (95% CI 0.4–4.8; n=2/148) versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally, stage is missing for about 48% of patients, and Finland lacks a cancer quality registry while lung cancer data reporting is incomplete and requires uniform recording instructions, the team recommends publishing per-county stage, drug-treatment, and MDT coding completeness.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "q:47c7e11303",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:82d365cd2c"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act sets no maximum time for a cancer suspicion and Finland lacks uniform diagnostic timetable guidance, the team recommends reporting referral-to-treatment access times using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions (16 cancers) and flagging stalled handovers until the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation with recommended time limits is carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:20d6ca414e",
          "q:ccda20dce9",
          "q:432c0e51d6",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "q:14dff3e002"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because referrals follow local instructions and mentor insight notes that weak referrals receive lower urgency ratings, the team recommends adopting a referral template and referring persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray (as in the KYS pathway document), plus naming a diagnostic contact person while the STM roadmap plans referral criteria (measure 2.5.2) and coordinator guidance (measure 1.2.3) by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:9a1cd194f5",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:050ee09ebe",
          "q:abcbb06ae3"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
